# Statics that stay in libc's per-process CORE rather than a member block
# (shared libc SP2 spec, section 4).  stdio's own state is _iob, a global,
# which the core holds anyway.  One unmangled name per line.
# findiop.c's sbuf: _smallbuf's initialiser takes its address, which a
# member block cannot give (the block is per-process and placed at load).
sbuf
